These assignment-only files select one strict optimization lane.  They do not
contain package fingerprints, ABI identities, generation IDs, or profile paths.
Those machine-specific values belong in generated Portage policy outside Git.

PGO mode files may be layered with bolt-capture-ready.conf or bolt-deploy.conf.
GCC BOLT lanes must additionally include bolt-gcc-ready.conf.  Active modes fail
unless the global bashrc receives an exact fingerprint, ABI, compiler lane, and
all profile identity inputs required by that mode.
